# Firebase configuration.
# These carry project ids and client keys. Firebase treats them as public by
# design — they ship inside every built app, and the real protection is the
# Firestore security rules, not secrecy. They are kept out of this public
# repository anyway so the project is not trivially discoverable, and fed to
# CI from repository secrets instead. Regenerate locally with:
#   flutterfire configure --project=munir-9360e
android/app/google-services.json
ios/Runner/GoogleService-Info.plist
lib/firebase_options.dart
firebase.json
